   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "REFERENCE PROMPTING - short form\n\n1. Save a character first: add H3 Character (save), feed it 3 anchor images\n   and a CLEAN 5-10s voice sample, give it a name + description, run once.\n   Refresh the browser, then pick it in H3 Character.\n\n2. H3 Character emits the wording AND the media:\n     subject_def / retention  -> H3 Scene Prompt\n     image_1..3               -> ref_image_1..3\n     voice                    -> ref_audio_1\n   `info` tells you how many image slots that character actually has.\n\n3. Shot syntax in H3 Scene Prompt:\n     shot description on its own line\n     > S1: dialogue for that shot\n     0:04 | pinned shot at four seconds\n\n4. Check the `lint` output on the node body before queueing. Red = the model\n   will do something you did not ask for.\n\nSECOND CHARACTER: add another H3 Character, set subject_index=2 and\npicture_offset = the first character's anchor count, wire into subject_def_2 /\nretention_2 and ref_image_4.. / ref_audio_2.\n\n640x1120 is the working resolution: 768x1152 produced cuts in chained clips,\n640x1120 did not. ref_image_size 'max' is truer identity at ~1.78x the time."
   ],
   "title": "How to use"
  }
